The consortium's journalists reviewed more than two thousand internal documents from the department and reported on them; the documents themselves were not published ([Meduza, 2026-05-07](https://meduza.io/amp/en/feature/2026/05/07/secret-gru-linked-department-at-top-russian-university-trains-hackers-and-saboteurs-investigation-finds)). The outlets attach the 2017 Macron campaign breach to different units: the Guardian lists it among Sandworm's accused operations ([The Guardian, 2026-05-07](https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/may/07/revealed-russia-top-secret-spy-school-hacking-western-electoral-interference)), while Le Monde accuses Fancy Bear (APT28), whose most recent alleged activity it names is the targeting of institutions organising the Paris 2024 Olympic Games ([Le Monde, 2026-05-07](https://www.lemonde.fr/en/m-le-mag/article/2026/05/07/moscow-s-bauman-university-the-clandestine-school-training-russian-hackers_6753208_117.html)); none of the cited outlets reports continuing 2025 to 2026 APT28 activity against EU government or election targets. The Metasploit training against US Department of Defense networks is VSquare's reporting ([VSquare, 2026-05-07](https://vsquare.org/welcome-to-the-gru-university-where-moscow-turns-students-into-spies-and-hackers-bauman-stupakov/)), and the one-month camp is one all students attend, per heise citing Der Spiegel ([heise online, 2026-05-07](https://www.heise.de/news/Cyberkrieg-Medien-zitieren-Interna-aus-Russlands-Geheimdienstausbildung-11285528.html)).
